🛑 What is Middleware? (Yeh kya hai?)
What: Middleware Express.js mein ek aisa Checkpost / Helper Function hota hai jo Client ke Request bhejane aur Server ke Response dene ke beech (middle) mein chalta hai.

Plaintext
Client ── Request ──> [ Checkpost / Middleware ] ──> Server Handler ──> Response
🤔 Why Middleware? (Zarurat kyun hai?)
Why: Agar Middleware nahi hoga, toh aapko har ek route function ke andar dublicate aur faltu code baar-baar likhna padega.

DRY Principle (Don't Repeat Yourself): Har route mein if (!name || !role) validation ya token verify karne ka code 10 baar likhne ki jagah, 1 middleware banao aur route ke beech mein laga do.

Security Check: Koi bina Login kiye sensitive data na dekh paye (Unauthorized request ko raste mein hi rok do).

Logging: Consoles/Logs track karne ke liye ki kaun kis URL ko hit kar raha hai.

⚙️ How it Works? (Kaise kaam karta hai aur kaise likhte hain?)
How: Express Middleware mein 3 Arguments hote hain: req (Request), res (Response), aur next (Agle step par bhejne ke liye function).

1. Logger Middleware (Global - Har Route Ke Liye)
JavaScript
// HOW TO WRITE: Global Middleware
app.use((req, res, next) => {
    console.log(`[LOG]: ${req.method} request aayi hai ${req.url} par`);
    
    next(); // 👈 Agle step par bhejne ke liye ZAROORI hai!
});
2. Validation Middleware (Route-Specific - Sirf Chuni hui API Ke Liye)
Step 1: Middleware Function Banao
JavaScript
// WHAT: Validation function jo check karega ki data sahi hai ya nahi
const validateUser = (req, res, next) => {
    const { name, role } = req.body;

    // WHY: Data missing hai toh aage jane hi mat do!
    if (!name || !role) {
        return res.status(400).json({ status: "fail", message: "Name aur Role dono chahiye!" });
    }

    next(); // HOW: Sab sahi hai, toh aage badho!
};
Step 2: Route Mein Beech Mein Laga Do
JavaScript
// HOW TO USE: Route handler se theek PEHLE pass kar do
app.post('/api/users', validateUser, (req, res) => {
    // Ab yahan validation ka tension zero hai!
    const newUser = req.body;
    users.push(newUser);
    res.status(201).json({ status: "success", data: newUser });
});
⚡ Ek Baat Hamesha Yaad Rakhna:
Middleware mein do hi raste hote hain:

Ya toh aap response wahi khatam kar do (return res.json(...)).

Ya fir aage jaane do (next()).

Agar next() call karna bhool gaye aur response bhi nahi diya, toh request hang (freeze) ho jayegi!




Problem -> ha smjh aa gya kitne type ke middleware hote hai and konsa kb kaha use krna hai yeh kese pata chlega yaar mujhe ?


Pure Express ecosystem mein 5 main types ke middlewares hote hain.Aapko kab aur kaun sa use karna hai, iski ek simple Decision Trick batata hoon.🎭 5 Types of Middlewares (What, Why, How)1. Built-in MiddlewaresWHAT: Express ke andar pehle se bane-banaye aate hain. Unhe create nahi karna padta, bas activate karna hota hai.WHY: Client jo data bhejta hai (JSON ya Form Data), Express use by-default nahi samajhta. Unhe parse karne ke liye.HOW & KAB USE KAREIN:Rule: Har Project ke bilkul top par server.js mein initialize kar do.JavaScriptapp.use(express.json()); // JSON data padhne ke liye
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true })); // Form data ke liye
app.use(express.static('public')); // Images/HTML serve karne ke liye
2. Application-Level (Global) MiddlewaresWHAT: Yeh app ki har single request par chalte hain, chahe route koi bhi ho (/api/users, /api/products, etc.).WHY: Aise kaam jo har request ke liye common hain — jaise Logging, Performance Tracker, CORS, ya Rate Limiting.HOW & KAB USE KAREIN:Rule: Jab aapko sabhi routes par same rule lagana ho. app.use() se lagate hain.JavaScript// Application-level logger
app.use((req, res, next) => {
    console.log(`[${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()}] ${req.method} ${req.url}`);
    next();
});
3. Router-Level / Route-Specific MiddlewaresWHAT: Yeh kisi khaas route (specific API) par lagte hain, sab par nahi.WHY: Selective security checks ke liye. (Jaise /api/admin par sirf Admin ko jane do, baaki log out ho jayein).HOW & KAB USE KAREIN:Rule: Route ke function signature mein beech mein pass kar do.JavaScriptconst checkAdmin = (req, res, next) => {
    if (req.headers.role === 'admin') next();
    else res.status(403).json({ message: "Forbidden! Admin only." });
};

// SIRF delete user waale route par laga:
app.delete('/api/users/:id', checkAdmin, (req, res) => {
    res.json({ message: "User deleted" });
});
4. Third-Party MiddlewaresWHAT: Yeh npm packages hote hain jo doosre developers ne banaye hain.WHY: Har cheez zero se code kyun karein jab production-tested solution ready hai?HOW & KAB USE KAREIN:npm i morgan cors helmetExamples:morgan: Professional Logging ke liye.cors: Frontend-Backend connection errors solve karne ke liye.helmet: App ki HTTP headers security badhane ke liye.JavaScriptimport cors from 'cors';
import morgan from 'morgan';

app.use(cors()); // Global API access allow karne ke liye
app.use(morgan('dev')); // Colorized terminal logs ke liye
5. Error-Handling MiddlewareWHAT: Yeh ek special middleware hai jisme 3 nahi, 4 arguments hote hain: (err, req, res, next).WHY: Agar kisi route mein code phat jaye (database error, undefined access), toh server crash hone se bachana aur clean Error Response dena.HOW & KAB USE KAREIN:Rule: Hamesha apne server.js ke sabse aakhri (bottom) mein likho, baaki saare routes ke baad.JavaScript// 4 arguments = Express ise samajh jata hai ki ye Error Middleware hai!
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
    console.error("🔥 Error Aaya Hai:", err.stack);
    res.status(500).json({
        status: 'error',
        message: err.message || 'Internal Server Error'
    });
});
💡 "Kaun Sa Kab Use Karna Hai?" (Cheat Sheet)Pehchanna bohot aasan hai! Apne aap se yeh 3 sawal poocho:SawalAnswer / SolutionKaun Sa Middleware?"Kya mujhe request data (req.body) read karna hai?"Built-inapp.use(express.json())"Kya yeh kaam har single request ke liye hona chahiye?"Application-Levelapp.use(logger)"Kya yeh check sirf selective / protected routes par lagna chahiye?"Route-Specificapp.post('/api', validation, controller)"Kya mujhe security, cors, ya professional logging chahiye?"Third-Partynpm install cors"Kya mere code mein error aaya aur server crash hone se rokna hai?"Error-Handlingapp.use((err, req, res, next) => ...)🎯 Sequence Order (Express Execution Flow)Express mein order bohot matter karta hai. Apne server.js ko hamesha is order mein structure karo:Plaintext1. Built-in Middlewares (express.json, cors)
   ↓
2. Global / Custom Middlewares (Morgan, Loggers)
   ↓
3. Application Routes (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
   ↓
